# What EAS Build uploads for the iPhone app (mobile/). When this file exists
# EAS uses it INSTEAD of every .gitignore, so it must also exclude what they
# do. Paths are relative to the REPOSITORY root (EAS copies from the git root).
#
# Written as a plain exclude list, NOT "/*" + "!/mobile/": EAS tests each
# path without a trailing slash, so a directory re-include like "!/mobile/"
# never matches and the archive came out as 80 bytes (build 3, cancelled).
# No trailing slashes below for the same reason.
#
# The phone build needs only mobile/ and the pure shared code in src/lib
# (mobile/metro.config.js) — everything heavy goes.

# Web app, docs and assets the phone never touches
/design_handoff_*
/docs
/public
/supabase
/scripts
/scratch
/*.zip
/src/app
/src/components
/src/hooks
/.next
/.vercel
/.claude
/coverage
/out
/build

# Never upload these, wherever they are
node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
*.tsbuildinfo
.env*
*.pem
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
.DS_Store
/mobile/ios
/mobile/android
